---
import fs from 'node:fs';
import path from 'node:path';
import { micromark } from 'micromark';
import { gfm, gfmHtml } from 'micromark-extension-gfm';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '/src/styles/design-system.css';

const root = process.cwd();
const designMdFull = fs.readFileSync(path.join(root, 'DESIGN.md'), 'utf-8');
const crdRaw = fs.readFileSync(
  path.join(root, 'src/system/design-system/components/selection-controls.crd.md'),
  'utf-8'
);

// Extract the "Design knowledge" section from DESIGN.md
const dsKnowledgeStart = designMdFull.indexOf('### Design knowledge');
const nextH3 = designMdFull.indexOf('\n### ', dsKnowledgeStart + 1);
const designMdExcerpt = designMdFull
  .slice(dsKnowledgeStart, nextH3 > dsKnowledgeStart ? nextH3 : undefined)
  .trim();

// Render CRD markdown to HTML using Astro's bundled micromark + GFM
const crdHtml = micromark(crdRaw, {
  extensions: [gfm()],
  htmlExtensions: [gfmHtml()],
});

const repoBase = 'https://github.com/wishayajeen/portfolio/blob/main';
const rawBase = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wishayajeen/portfolio/main';
---

<Layout
  title="Your Design System Has a New User: AI — Jeen"
  description="XConf Americas 2026 talk companion. How structured design knowledge — DESIGN.md routing and Component Requirements Documents — makes design systems accessible to AI agents."
>

  <!-- Sticky topbar -->
  <div class="ds-topbar">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Jeen.work</a>
    <span class="ds-topbar-sep">/</span>
    <span class="ds-topbar-title">Work</span>
    <span class="ds-topbar-sep">/</span>
    <span class="ds-topbar-title">XConf Americas 2026</span>
  </div>

  <!-- Dark page header -->
  <div class="xconf-header">
    <div class="xconf-header-inner">
      <p class="article-eyebrow">XConf Americas 2026 · Nov 5, 2026 · Talk</p>
      <h1 class="xconf-title">Your Design System<br>Has a New User: AI</h1>
      <p class="xconf-intro">
        Design systems are built for humans — component libraries, style guides, Figma documentation. But when AI agents start
        reading them to implement features, the rules change. This talk explores how to structure design knowledge so AI
        agents can discover rules, apply constraints correctly, and produce work that matches the system's intent. The result
        is a design system that works for both audiences without duplicating information.
      </p>
      <div class="xconf-recording-placeholder">
        <span class="xconf-recording-icon" aria-hidden="true">▶</span>
        Talk recording — coming soon
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Page content -->
  <main class="ds-page">

    <!-- Section 01: DESIGN.md -->
    <section class="ds-section">
      <div class="ds-section-header">
        <span class="ds-section-num">01</span>
        <h2 class="ds-section-title">Making design knowledge navigable</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="xconf-prose">
        A design system documented only in Figma, or scattered across wiki pages and Notion docs, is invisible to an AI
        agent. <code class="ds-code">DESIGN.md</code> acts as a machine-readable routing map — it tells an agent where to
        find tokens, component requirements, architectural rules, and constraints, without duplicating any of them. One
        origin per decision; the map just points.
      </p>
      <div class="xconf-file-card">
        <div class="xconf-file-card-header">
          <span class="xconf-file-name">DESIGN.md — Design knowledge section</span>
          <div class="xconf-file-links">
            <a
              href={`${repoBase}/DESIGN.md`}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="xconf-file-link"
            >GitHub →</a>
            <a
              href={`${rawBase}/DESIGN.md`}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="xconf-file-link"
            >Raw →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <pre class="xconf-code-block">{designMdExcerpt}</pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 02: CRD -->
    <section class="ds-section">
      <div class="ds-section-header">
        <span class="ds-section-num">02</span>
        <h2 class="ds-section-title">Component Requirements Documents</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="xconf-prose">
        Component documentation typically covers appearance and props. A Component Requirements Document (CRD) adds the layer
        that matters most for AI agents: <em>why</em> a component exists, <em>when</em> to use it versus alternatives, and
        which product-specific decisions apply. The document below is a real example from this repository — created for the
        talk using a fictional product called Acme to illustrate the format.
      </p>
      <div class="xconf-file-card">
        <div class="xconf-file-card-header">
          <span class="xconf-file-name">selection-controls.crd.md</span>
          <div class="xconf-file-links">
            <a
              href={`${repoBase}/src/system/design-system/components/selection-controls.crd.md`}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="xconf-file-link"
            >GitHub →</a>
            <a
              href={`${rawBase}/src/system/design-system/components/selection-controls.crd.md`}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="xconf-file-link"
            >Raw →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="xconf-md-body" set:html={crdHtml} />
      </div>
      <p class="xconf-credit">
        CRD approach inspired by <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JeJhPtsbIGA" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="xconf-credit-link">Cassie Groos</a>. Example adapted for this talk.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 03: Before/After -->
    <section class="ds-section">
      <div class="ds-section-header">
        <span class="ds-section-num">03</span>
        <h2 class="ds-section-title">Notification preferences: before and after</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="xconf-prose">
        The comparison below illustrates an AI-generated notification screen (using checkboxes) alongside the
        design-system intended version (using switches). In the Acme product, notification settings take effect
        immediately — no submit button, no confirmation step. The CRD establishes that Switch is the required control
        for this context; Checkbox implies deferred submission that never arrives.
      </p>
      <p class="xconf-disclaimer">
        This is an illustrative comparison. It does not represent the output of a specific AI model or a measured experiment result.
      </p>

      <div class="xconf-comparison">

        <!-- Before: AI-generated -->
        <div class="xconf-panel">
          <div class="xconf-panel-head">
            <span class="xconf-panel-label xconf-panel-label--before">AI-generated example</span>
            <span class="xconf-drift-badge">Control-pattern drift</span>
          </div>
          <div class="xconf-screen">
            <p class="xconf-screen-title">Notification preferences</p>

            <div class="xconf-setting-row">
              <div class="xconf-setting-text">
                <label class="xconf-setting-label" for="before-email">Email notifications</label>
                <span class="xconf-setting-desc">Receive updates and alerts via email</span>
              </div>
              <label class="xconf-checkbox" for="before-email">
                <input type="checkbox" id="before-email" checked aria-label="Email notifications" />
                <span class="xconf-checkbox-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              </label>
            </div>

            <div class="xconf-setting-row">
              <div class="xconf-setting-text">
                <label class="xconf-setting-label" for="before-sms">SMS notifications</label>
                <span class="xconf-setting-desc">Get text messages for important alerts</span>
              </div>
              <label class="xconf-checkbox" for="before-sms">
                <input type="checkbox" id="before-sms" checked aria-label="SMS notifications" />
                <span class="xconf-checkbox-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              </label>
            </div>

            <div class="xconf-setting-row">
              <div class="xconf-setting-text">
                <label class="xconf-setting-label" for="before-push">Push notifications</label>
                <span class="xconf-setting-desc">Browser and mobile push alerts</span>
              </div>
              <label class="xconf-checkbox" for="before-push">
                <input type="checkbox" id="before-push" aria-label="Push notifications" />
                <span class="xconf-checkbox-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              </label>
            </div>

            <div class="xconf-setting-row">
              <div class="xconf-setting-text">
                <label class="xconf-setting-label" for="before-marketing">Marketing emails</label>
                <span class="xconf-setting-desc">Product updates and announcements</span>
              </div>
              <label class="xconf-switch" for="before-marketing">
                <input type="checkbox" role="switch" id="before-marketing" checked aria-label="Marketing emails" />
                <span class="xconf-switch-track" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              </label>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="xconf-panel-note">Checkboxes imply selections are applied on submission. These settings take effect immediately — there is no submit step.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- After: Design-system intended -->
        <div class="xconf-panel">
          <div class="xconf-panel-head">
            <span class="xconf-panel-label xconf-panel-label--after">Design-system intended</span>
          </div>
          <div class="xconf-screen">
            <p class="xconf-screen-title">Notification preferences</p>

            <div class="xconf-setting-row">
              <div class="xconf-setting-text">
                <label class="xconf-setting-label" for="after-email">Email notifications</label>
                <span class="xconf-setting-desc">Receive updates and alerts via email</span>
              </div>
              <label class="xconf-switch" for="after-email">
                <input type="checkbox" role="switch" id="after-email" checked aria-label="Email notifications" />
                <span class="xconf-switch-track" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              </label>
            </div>

            <div class="xconf-setting-row">
              <div class="xconf-setting-text">
                <label class="xconf-setting-label" for="after-sms">SMS notifications</label>
                <span class="xconf-setting-desc">Get text messages for important alerts</span>
              </div>
              <label class="xconf-switch" for="after-sms">
                <input type="checkbox" role="switch" id="after-sms" checked aria-label="SMS notifications" />
                <span class="xconf-switch-track" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              </label>
            </div>

            <div class="xconf-setting-row">
              <div class="xconf-setting-text">
                <label class="xconf-setting-label" for="after-push">Push notifications</label>
                <span class="xconf-setting-desc">Browser and mobile push alerts</span>
              </div>
              <label class="xconf-switch" for="after-push">
                <input type="checkbox" role="switch" id="after-push" aria-label="Push notifications" />
                <span class="xconf-switch-track" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              </label>
            </div>

            <div class="xconf-setting-row">
              <div class="xconf-setting-text">
                <label class="xconf-setting-label" for="after-marketing">Marketing emails</label>
                <span class="xconf-setting-desc">Product updates and announcements</span>
              </div>
              <label class="xconf-switch" for="after-marketing">
                <input type="checkbox" role="switch" id="after-marketing" checked aria-label="Marketing emails" />
                <span class="xconf-switch-track" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              </label>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="xconf-panel-note">Switches correctly convey that these settings take effect immediately, without a submit step.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

  <!-- Footer -->
  <footer class="ds-footer">
    <div class="ds-footer-inner">
      <a href="/#work" class="ds-footer-link xconf-footer-link">← Back to work</a>
      <a href="/work/xconf-americas-2026" class="ds-footer-link xconf-footer-link" onclick="window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'});return false;">↑ Top</a>
    </div>
  </footer>

</Layout>

<style>
  /* ── Page header (dark) ── */
  .xconf-header {
    background: var(--bg-dark);
    padding: var(--space-16) var(--space-6) var(--space-12);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(250, 250, 250, 0.08);
  }
  .xconf-header-inner {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .xconf-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    line-height: var(--leading-tight);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
    color: var(--fg-on-dark-primary);
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-6);
  }
  .xconf-intro {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    color: var(--fg-on-dark-secondary);
    max-width: 680px;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  .xconf-recording-placeholder {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--fg-on-dark-label);
    border: 1px solid rgba(250, 250, 250, 0.15);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }
  .xconf-recording-icon {
    font-size: 10px;
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  /* ── Page content top padding ── */
  .ds-page { padding-top: var(--space-16); }

  /* ── Section prose ── */
  .xconf-prose {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    color: var(--fg-secondary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    max-width: 720px;
  }
  .xconf-prose em { color: var(--fg-primary); font-style: italic; }
  .xconf-disclaimer {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--fg-secondary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-5);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--fg-tertiary);
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius-xs) var(--radius-xs) 0;
    max-width: 620px;
  }

  /* ── File card ── */
  .xconf-file-card {
    border: var(--border-primary);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
  }
  .xconf-file-card-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-5);
    background: var(--bg-dark);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(250, 250, 250, 0.08);
  }
  .xconf-file-name {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--fg-on-dark-secondary);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .xconf-file-links {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }
  .xconf-file-link {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--fg-on-dark-accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    box-shadow: none; /* override global a {} */
    transition: opacity var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }
  .xconf-file-link:hover { opacity: 0.8; color: var(--fg-on-dark-accent); box-shadow: none; }
  .xconf-code-block {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--fg-primary);
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    padding: var(--space-6);
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 0;
    white-space: pre;
    tab-size: 2;
  }

  /* ── Rendered CRD markdown ── */
  .xconf-md-body {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    color: var(--fg-secondary);
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    padding: var(--space-8) var(--space-6);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .xconf-md-body h1,
  .xconf-md-body h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--fg-primary);
    margin: var(--space-8) 0 var(--space-3);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-2);
    border-bottom: var(--border-subtle);
  }
  .xconf-md-body h1:first-child,
  .xconf-md-body h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .xconf-md-body h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--fg-primary);
    margin: var(--space-6) 0 var(--space-2);
  }
  .xconf-md-body p {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
    max-width: 72ch;
  }
  .xconf-md-body ul,
  .xconf-md-body ol {
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }
  .xconf-md-body li { margin-bottom: var(--space-1); }
  .xconf-md-body blockquote {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--border-accent);
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-5);
    margin: var(--space-4) 0;
    background: rgba(243, 254, 82, 0.05); /* subtle yellow tint from --color-yellow — accent callout */
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius-xs) var(--radius-xs) 0;
    color: var(--fg-secondary);
  }
  .xconf-md-body blockquote p { margin: 0; }
  .xconf-md-body code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    background: var(--bg-surface-raised);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
    border: var(--border-subtle);
    color: var(--fg-primary);
  }
  .xconf-md-body pre {
    background: var(--bg-surface-raised);
    border: var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
    padding: var(--space-4);
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: var(--space-4) 0;
  }
  .xconf-md-body pre code {
    background: none;
    border: none;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .xconf-md-body table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    margin: var(--space-4) 0;
  }
  .xconf-md-body th {
    text-align: left;
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-primary);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--fg-primary);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .xconf-md-body td {
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
    border-bottom: var(--border-subtle);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .xconf-md-body a {
    color: var(--fg-primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    box-shadow: none; /* override global a {} */
  }
  .xconf-md-body a:hover { opacity: 0.7; box-shadow: none; }
  .xconf-md-body hr {
    border: none;
    border-top: var(--border-subtle);
    margin: var(--space-8) 0;
  }

  /* ── Before/after comparison ── */
  .xconf-comparison {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }
  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .xconf-comparison { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  .xconf-panel {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }
  .xconf-panel-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .xconf-panel-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
    padding: 3px var(--space-3);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  }
  .xconf-panel-label--before {
    background: rgba(255, 68, 68, 0.1); /* subtle tint from --color-error #FF4444 */
    color: var(--color-error);
  }
  .xconf-panel-label--after {
    background: rgba(61, 254, 135, 0.1); /* subtle tint from --color-success #3DFE87 */
    color: #1a8a4a; /* darkened for contrast on light bg — #3DFE87 fails AA */
  }
  .xconf-drift-badge {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-error);
    background: rgba(255, 68, 68, 0.08);
    padding: 2px var(--space-2);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  }

  /* Mock notification screen */
  .xconf-screen {
    border: var(--border-primary);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: var(--bg-surface-raised);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
  }
  .xconf-screen-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--fg-primary);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-5);
  }
  .xconf-setting-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    padding: var(--space-4) 0;
    border-bottom: var(--border-subtle);
  }
  .xconf-setting-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .xconf-setting-text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3px;
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .xconf-setting-label {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--fg-primary);
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .xconf-setting-desc {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--fg-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }
  .xconf-panel-note {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    color: var(--fg-secondary);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── Custom checkbox — min 44×44px touch target ── */
  .xconf-checkbox {
    position: relative;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-width: 44px;
    min-height: 44px;
    cursor: pointer;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .xconf-checkbox input[type="checkbox"] {
    position: absolute;
    opacity: 0;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    margin: 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    z-index: 1;
  }
  .xconf-checkbox-box {
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    border: var(--border-primary);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
    background: var(--bg-surface-raised);
    position: relative;
    transition: background var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .xconf-checkbox input[type="checkbox"]:checked + .xconf-checkbox-box {
    background: var(--fg-primary);
  }
  .xconf-checkbox input[type="checkbox"]:checked + .xconf-checkbox-box::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 5px;
    top: 2px;
    width: 6px;
    height: 10px;
    border: 2px solid white;
    border-top: none;
    border-left: none;
    transform: rotate(45deg);
  }
  .xconf-checkbox input[type="checkbox"]:focus-visible + .xconf-checkbox-box {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-focus);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

